<Section id="styling" title="3. Styling your Shapes">
To colour our shapes based on genre we use an **object** as a lookup table - think of it like a **dictionary**: you look up a word (the genre) and get back its definition (the colour). Each line is a **key** (the genre) paired with a **value** (the colour):

```svelte
/// file: Colour map
let genreColors = {
	'Dance pop': '#E75B2B',
	Pop: '#DB1E24',
	'Hip-hop/R&B': '#F9B806',
	'Acoustic/Folk': '#3091B9',
	Other: '#E032A3',
	EDM: '#53DC41'
};
```

To look one up, we put the key in **square brackets**:

```svelte
/// file: Looking up a colour
genreColors['Dance pop']; // "#E75B2B"
genreColors[row["genre"]]; // the colour for this row's genre
```

Now do it in your exercise:

<Exercise file="5-drawing-an-entire-dataset.svelte" solution="5-styled.svelte" bleed>
	<DrawingEntireDataset />
	{#snippet result()}
		<ColoredGridDemo />
