</Exercise>

{#snippet sidebar()}

Paste this colour map into your file:

```svelte
/// file: Colour map
let genreColors = {
	'Dance pop': '#E75B2B',
	Pop: '#DB1E24',
	'Hip-hop/R&B': '#F9B806',
	'Acoustic/Folk': '#3091B9',
	Other: '#E032A3',
	EDM: '#53DC41'
};
```

> [!Note] New words
> - **object**: a set of **key → value** pairs, like a dictionary.
> - **key**: what you look up (here, the genre).
> - **value**: what you get back (here, the colour).
> - **lookup**: read a value with square brackets — `genreColors[row["genre"]]`.

**Colour the cell and the label**

```svelte
/// file: Fills
<rect ... fill={genreColors[row["genre"]]} />
<circle ... fill={genreColors[row["genre"]]} />
```

